<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto Pérez Molina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto Pérez Molina (born 1950) is a retired Guatemalan general who was president from 2012 to 2015. A former head of military intelligence and a signatory of the 1996 peace accords, he was elected on promises of firm action against crime. In 2015 investigations by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-commission-against-impunity-in-guatemala">International Commission against Impunity in Guatemala</a> into the La Línea customs fraud forced his resignation and arrest, and he was later convicted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-perez-molina.jpg" alt="Otto Pérez Molina" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Guatemala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foto_oficial_de_Presidente_Otto_Molina_Perez_(cropped_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
